Nehrim

Oblivion conversion mod - some Oblivion mods may be applicable, check first.
Engine is notorious for crashing, see about setting up autosaves using full saves (assume same rules as modded Skyrim apply - no quicksaves, only full, no overwriting old saves, ideally no reloading)

Oblivion should support 21:9 resolution, though with harmless glitches in loading screens (which are patched)

Use protontricks/winetricks to install d3dx9_43 libraries

ENBoost is not to be used with Linux - instead look into things that DXVK and wine do. https://github.com/rockerbacon/modorganizer2-linux-installer/issues/177
	Ensure you set this in the game launch options, so it is large address aware: WINE_FORCE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE=1 %command%
	Configure dxvk.conf with d3d9.evictManagedOnUnlock

It is said that codecs packs should be removed - caused freezes every minute for someone
It is said that "Memory Purge" should be turned off, caused crashes when loading new areas

Sound was giving issues (looping bug, no ambient noise)
------------
Installation
------------
mkdir /home/$USER/Games/Nehrim-wineGE
WINEPREFIX=/home/$USER/Games/Nehrim-wineGE winecfg
export WINEPREFIX=/home/$USER/Games/Nehrim-wineGE
WINEPREFIX=/home/$USER/Games/Nehrim-wineGE winetricks --force d3dcompiler_43 d3dx9_43
WINEPREFIX=/home/$USER/Games/Nehrim-wineGE wine /home/$USER/Stuff/Games/GoG-installers/Nehrim:AtFate\'sEdge/setup_nehrim_at_fates_edge_1.0.0.0_\(61681\).exe
Installer runs, do not launch when done.
WINEPREFIX=/home/$USER/Games/Nehrim-wineGE wine "/home/$USER/location/of/Mo2_Installer/Mod.Organizer-xxxxx.exe"
Once the installer finishes, uncheck the launch checkbox and close the installer
Add MO2 to Lutris, choose wine runner. 
Add  WINE_FORCE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE=1 to the Environment variables
Launch MO2 - create a portable instance, point it to the Nehrim install location (path of the executables folder) (you may have to enter the path manually)
Once MO2 is up, go to executables, Oblivion.exe, (it should have the Daedric O character, but say 'Nehrim' next to it in the menu) Force Load Libraries > Configure Libraries. Ensure the checkbox on the line that says Oblivion.exe and obse_1_2_416.dll is checked
Once this is checked, launching Oblivion.exe will load the obse script extender. Do NOT use obse_loader.exe to start the game
WINEPREFIX=/home/$USER/Games/Nehrim-wineGE wine "/home/$USER/Games/Nehrim/NehrimMods/Wrye Bash 311 - Installer-2-311-1685294836.exe"
Then add wrye bash in Mo2. Ensure it loads plugins placed in MO2

Open the TES4edit archive, and copy 'Edit Scripts', 'TES4Edit.exe', and 'TES4EditQuickAutoClean.exe' to the Nehrim Data folder
Now go to MO2, and add executables for Tes4Edit and Tes4EditQAC, connect them to the proper .exe files
If TES4Edit is not loading the plugins in MO2, configure it's executable options to start in the main Nehrim folder. 
If TES4Edit cannot find the .ini, create the 'My Games/Oblivion' folder in your wine c_drive docuemtns folder, and copy the oblivion.ini file from your Nehrim folder over

Install all regular plugins, etc. Sort load order
[landscape LOD textures - needs manual install, refer to Readme]
[Easiest to install grass fix manually as well]

Setting dxvk.conf (replace enboost) Take the dxvk.conf file, and place it in the Main game directory (where all the exe's are). Add this line to it: d3d9.evictManagedOnUnlock = True

Unpack BethINI somewhere in the c_drive
BethINI: WINEPREFIX=/home/$USER/Games/Nehrim-wineGE wine /location/of/BethINI.exe
Select default,(let it load), Ultra (let it load), recomended tweaks (let it load), then save and exit

Decided not to mess with ENB this time - too much stuff can break, too much messing with stuff

Launch the game from the NehrimLauncher.exe, from in MO2

Set fDlgFocus to 15 in oblivion.ini - disables the dialog zoom
Autosaves should be off when you disable the three settings in the oblivion.ini

Fix no sound effects:
Unpack the BSA Extractor somewhere, and run
WINEPREFIX=/home/$USER/Games/Nehrim-wineGE wine /home/$USER/Games/Nehrim-wineGE/drive_c/BAE/bae.exe
Drop the "N - Sounds.bsa" into it and extract somewhere. You should have a folder structure like this: sound/fx/ , and in the fx directory should be many folders with sound effects. Copy this sound folder into the Nehrim Data folder - the structure should look like this: ******/drive_c/GOG Games/Nehrim at Fate's Edge GoG/Data/sound/fx/(all manner of sound effect folders)

Ensure that the can't pick up pickaxes/shovel bug is gone.

On game startup:
	click the menu that asks if you want to go back to default Nehrim settings - choose no.
	disable autosaves (Simple Saves Plus replaces autosave - implements an automatic regular save feature)
	configure Simple Saves Plus
	Character creation Celis
